cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyANTI-FASc, please cite the software using the citation metadata below."
type: software
title: "pyANTI-FASc"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-19"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20287413"
url: "https://github.com/antonioscalaunina/pyANTI-FASc"
repository-code: "https://github.com/antonioscalaunina/pyANTI-FASc"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
abstract: >-
  pyANTI-FASc is a Python implementation of ANTI-FASc (Automatic Numerical
  Tsunami Initial conditions: on-the-Fly rupture Areas and earthquake Scenarios)
  for the fast generation of large ensembles of stochastic slip distributions on
  complex non-planar fault geometries. The generated slip models can be used as
  initial conditions for tsunami simulations in Probabilistic Tsunami Hazard
  Assessment (PTHA) and real-time Probabilistic Tsunami Forecasting (PTF).
keywords:
  - tsunami
  - earthquake scenarios
  - stochastic slip distributions
  - complex fault geometries
  - non-planar fault geometries
  - Probabilistic Tsunami Hazard Assessment
  - PTHA
  - Probabilistic Tsunami Forecasting
  - PTF
  - Python
  - Docker
